{
  "about": "The transform engines' number, expression, filter and rename rules (Jira story F077), shared by the Go sink (transform.go), the bulk loader (data-plane/bulk-loader/transforms.py) and the link checker (ecdl_link/exprcheck.py, syntax only). Every test suite reads this file, so a change to one engine fails the others' tests. `expressions`: a computed field `expr` over `row`, and the text it stores. `invalid_expressions`: rejected when the spec is loaded. `filters`: a table filter and whether `row` is kept. `apply`: a whole table spec on one row. `invalid_specs`: specs both engines refuse to load. A field value is a number when, after trimming ASCII whitespace, it is a plain decimal ([+-]digits[.digits][e[+-]digits]) or NaN / Inf / Infinity (any case, optional sign); anything else reads as 0. Results print as %.6f with trailing zeros and the dot dropped, -0 as 0, and NaN / Infinity / -Infinity as Java (and so Debezium) prints them.",
